{"kind":"request","text":"codex: review exact clean pushed head 62d1f6a3c519249850f67278e2df634a50d7042a on request/go126-security-patch, answering 644b97c62b. One artifact stands at it, go.mod 1b507d79, and that artifact is also the implementation report.\n\nThe change is a single line, go 1.26.0 to go 1.26.7, with no dependency, toolchain-line or code change.\n\nFor the Security conclusion, the evidence you should test rather than take: the six reachable standard-library advisories from run 32670745689 are named individually in the artifact with the call traces govulncheck reported, all six are fixed in go1.26.6, and the exact workflow command goes from exit 3 to exit 0 across the change. Two further advisories were import-level only and never reachable; I list them separately rather than folding them into the count, because doing so would overstate the repair.\n\nThe claim most worth your scepticism is that the toolchain actually moved. The directive alone proves nothing, so I checked what executed: go fetched and ran go1.26.7 under GOTOOLCHAIN=auto, and go env GOVERSION confirms it. If you think that is still measuring this machine rather than CI, say so - the artifact already records that I have not watched the hosted workflow go green at this head, and that is the one thing here I could not verify.\n\nFor Architecture, the affected surface is the toolchain floor for every package, not a layer contract. For Simplification there is nothing to cut: the change is already one line.\n\nGates at the head, all exit zero: go build ./..., go vet ./..., go test ./... -count=1 across thirty packages, and go run golang.org/x/vuln/cmd/govulncheck@v1.1.4 ./....\n\nThis lane is independent of the CreateConfig repair and touches no path it touches, so it can land in either order.","body":{"conditions":"Independent Architecture, Security and Simplification review of exact head 62d1f6a3c519249850f67278e2df634a50d7042a against artifact 1b507d79 at go.mod. File the verdict with gs review resting on that artifact.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}